# chibi-tar: give `user-name` and `group-name` the portable branch they lack
#
# `chibi/tar.sld` gets four names from the host: `user-name`, `group-name`,
# `user-information` and `group-information`. Its `cond-expand` has a `chibi`
# branch, which imports them from `(chibi system)` -- C-backed upstream -- and
# a `chicken` branch, which imports `posix` and defines stand-ins for the
# first two. There is no `else`. On any other implementation the library
# loads and `make-tar` then fails with `user-name` unbound. See #404.
#
# **The rewrite is the author's own, moved one branch over.** The two
# `define`s below are the CHICKEN branch's, character for character. The only
# text that is new is `user-information` and `group-information` answering
# `#f`, "no such user", where CHICKEN's `posix` would consult the password
# database Patina has no access to.
#
# **It changes nothing the suite measures.** The package already treats an
# unknown user as ordinary: `file-owner-or-nobody` is
# `(or (user-name (user-information uid)) "nobody")`, and the stand-in takes a
# non-pair to `"nobody"` by itself. So every tar record Patina builds is owned
# by "nobody", which is a value the format and the package both expect, and no
# assertion reads a looked-up name -- the suite sets the owners it checks
# (`"bob"`, `"john"`, `"smith"`) itself.
#
# **Why a patch and not a bundled `(chibi system)`.** Patina does not ship
# chibi's libraries as a rule, and this one could not be honest if it did: a
# `(chibi system)` without a user database is the same stand-in wearing the
# real library's name. The import also sits under the `chibi` feature, which
# Patina does not and should not claim, so the `cond-expand` would need
# patching either way.
#
# This patch alone does not make the package pass. Behind `user-name`,
# chibi-binary-record writes its string fields to a bytevector port with
# `write-string`, which Patina refused until the same change that added this
# file; that was a Patina inconsistency and was fixed in Patina, not patched
# here.
#
# Measured after, with both: 15 of 15 assertions pass on both backends, where
# the package had stopped before its first.
diff -ruN a/chibi/tar.sld b/chibi/tar.sld
--- a/chibi/tar.sld
+++ b/chibi/tar.sld
@@ -14,6 +14,12 @@
     (import posix)
     (begin
       (define (user-name x) (if (pair? x) (car x) "nobody"))
+      (define (group-name x) (if (pair? x) (car x) "nobody"))))
+   (else
+    (begin
+      (define (user-information x) #f)
+      (define (group-information x) #f)
+      (define (user-name x) (if (pair? x) (car x) "nobody"))
       (define (group-name x) (if (pair? x) (car x) "nobody")))))
   (export
    ;; basic
